1	/*
2	 * Test stub for scripts/macos-bundle-swap-e2e.sh. Compiled at CI time
3	 * via clang and dropped into each test .app bundle as Contents/MacOS/
4	 * freenet-bin.
5	 *
6	 * Rationale: the updater script (scripts/macos-bundle-updater.sh) uses
7	 * `pgrep -f "^${bundle}/Contents/MacOS/"` to detect the running Freenet
8	 * process. That pattern assumes the kernel invoked a real Mach-O at the
9	 * bundle path, so the process command line begins with that path. A
10	 * shell-script freenet-bin does not satisfy this: the shebang hands off
11	 * to /bin/bash and the process command line starts with `/bin/bash`
